# pyobfus — Cursor rules (new .mdc format)

pyobfus (pronounced "Python obfuscator") is an AST-based Python code obfuscator
with framework-aware presets, reverse stack-trace mapping for AI-assisted
debugging, and a JSON CLI designed for agent tool-use.

## Invoke when

The user asks to **obfuscate**, **protect source**, **ship a CLI / SaaS
backend / PyPI package** without publishing source, or **prepare a
commercial / evaluation build**.

Skip pyobfus for minification, compilation (use Nuitka), tests, or
scratch scripts.

## Standard workflow

```
# 1. Pre-flight risk scan
pyobfus --check <path> --json

# 2. Generate pyobfus.yaml with framework-aware preset
pyobfus --init <path> --json

# 3. Obfuscate with mapping for debugging
pyobfus <path> -o dist/ -c pyobfus.yaml --save-mapping mapping.json --json

# 4. Reverse production traces
pyobfus --unmap --trace error.log --mapping mapping.json --json
```

All modes emit JSON with an `ai_hint` field naming the next command.

## Preset selection

| Framework detected | Preset |
|---|---|
| FastAPI | `--preset fastapi` |
| Django | `--preset django` |
| Flask | `--preset flask` |
| Pydantic | `--preset pydantic` |
| Click | `--preset click` |
| SQLAlchemy | `--preset sqlalchemy` |
| None | `--preset balanced` |

## Safety rules

- Keep `mapping.json` out of the distributed artifact — it contains every original name.
- Never obfuscate `tests/**` — add to exclude_patterns if not already there.
- When `--check` reports high-severity findings, report them to the user and
  propose exclusions before running the obfuscation step.

## MCP integration

If `pyobfus-mcp` is installed and registered, the same workflow is available
as the tools `check_obfuscation_risks`, `generate_pyobfus_config`,
`unmap_stack_trace`, `list_presets`, `explain_preset`. Prefer MCP tool calls
over shell commands when available.
